    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class. The full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nThe implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I changed to satisfy the soft-duplicate specification:\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen a new owner is not a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while carrying a **different** telephone, it is still created, and the response now reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id \u2014 otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These regenerate `OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persistent `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) columns with getters/setters. They're snapshotted at creation and MapStruct auto-maps them onto `OwnerDto` (matching field names).\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table. Tests use the hsqldb profile.\n\n4. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `assignPossibleDuplicate(...)`, invoked in `addOwner` right after the hard-duplicate rejection. It scans existing owners for one with the same postcode and case-insensitively-equal last name but a different normalized telephone, picks the earliest by id if several match, and snapshots the flag/id onto the owner (false / null when none match).\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
